# 4. Connection State Machine

## States

- Requested
- Active
- Rejected
- Disconnected
- Blocked

## Flow

```
Requested → Active → Disconnected
     ↓          ↓
  Rejected    Blocked
```

## Allowed Transitions

| From | To | Actor |
|---|---|---|
| (none) | Requested | Pharmacy |
| Requested | Active | Stockist |
| Requested | Rejected | Stockist |
| Requested | Cancelled/Closed | Pharmacy cancel request (terminal of request) |
| Active | Disconnected | Pharmacy or Stockist (permitted) |
| Active | Blocked | Stockist / Admin (policy) |
| Blocked | Active | Stockist / Admin (unblock) |
| Disconnected | Requested | Pharmacy (new request) |

## Forbidden

- Rejected → Active without new request
- Requested → Disconnected
- Self-connection
- Duplicate Active connection for same pair

## Side Effects

- Active enables catalogue trade and ordering.
- Non-Active blocks new orders.
- Historical documents unaffected by disconnect/block.

## Timeout

- Requested aged beyond SLA → reminder; optional auto-expire to closed request if policy enabled

