# Cross-Entity Transition Coordination

Some transitions are coupled.

| Trigger | Coupled Effects |
|---|---|
| Connection Active→Disconnected | Block new Orders; existing in-flight follow policy |
| Business→Suspended | Block new trade transitions into Pending orders |
| Order→Accepted | May reserve Inventory |
| Order→Cancelled/Rejected | Release reservations |
| Delivery→Delivered | Order→Delivered/Partially Delivered |
| Payment→Approved | Invoice→Partially Paid/Paid |
| Return→Approved | Credit Note issuance eligible |
| Credit applied | Invoice outstanding reduced; Credit remaining reduced |
| Batch→Expired | Inventory sellability reduced; allocation blocked |

No coupled effect may violate the target entity's own state machine.

---

# Forbidden Global Patterns

1. Skipping verification to trade
2. Jumping financial documents backwards into editable draft after issue/payment
3. Using chat/notifications as status authorities
4. Negative inventory via transition side effects
5. Delivering expired batches via dispatch transition
6. Reverse from Closed/Locked without formal controlled reopen policy
7. Silent status changes without actor + timestamp

